================================================================================
LICENSING NOTES (read before running this in production)
================================================================================

Nothing in this project needs a paid license to run as shipped. The following
points are disclosed so that you can decide for your own deployment.

  LiteLLM
  - The official image installs the "litellm-enterprise" Python package
    (proprietary, BerriAI Enterprise license; its terms say production use
    requires a BerriAI subscription). LiteLLM's open-source proxy imports it and
    calls into it on every request even when no license is set; LiteLLM
    publishes this image as its free, self-hostable gateway. If this matters for
    you, confirm with BerriAI (info@berri.ai).
  - Admin UI single sign-on is free for up to 5 users. LiteLLM counts the rows
    of its own user table (people who signed in to the LiteLLM UI, plus the
    dashboard's viewer account); from the 6th, an SSO login to the LiteLLM UI is
    refused with HTTP 403 unless LITELLM_LICENSE is set. Open WebUI users are
    end users in LiteLLM and do not count; chat is not affected.
  - Per-team logging ("./platformctl onboard-team --langfuse-secret", which
    calls POST /team/<id>/callback) is documented by LiteLLM as an Enterprise
    feature. In the pinned version the code is MIT and has no license check.
  - These are documented as Enterprise-only and are not used by this project:
    guardrails or policies per key/team, team admins, organizations,
    model_max_budget, tag budgets, key regeneration, team-scoped models, JWT/OIDC
    authentication of API calls, audit logs. Check
    https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/enterprise before enabling them.
  - GET /health/license on the proxy shows the license state ("community"
    without a license).

  Data sent to third parties by default
  - Langfuse sends anonymous usage telemetry to Langfuse (PostHog) every 12
    hours: version, counts of projects, traces and observations, and up to 30
    user email domains with their counts. Set TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false in
    platform/services/langfuse/helm-values.yaml (langfuse.additionalEnv) to stop it.
  - vLLM sends anonymous usage statistics to stats.vllm.ai unless
    VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1 is set on the model server.
  - ClickHouse's default server configuration sends crash reports to
    crash.clickhouse.com.
  - Open WebUI's image turns its telemetry off.

